      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so im trying to give a lambda function access to write logs to an s3 bucket but im getting an access denied error. i thought i fixed it but it still isnt working. here is the policy i'm using:\n\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"s3:PutObject\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::my-app-logs-bucket/*\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\ncan u see what im doing wrong?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're very close, but there's a subtle \"goblin\" in your policy that's causing the access denied error. The resource ARN you provided is `arn:aws:s3:::my-app-logs-bucket/*`, which is correct for allowing writes to objects inside the bucket. However, the issue often lies in the **bucket policy** itself or the **IAM role** attached to your Lambda function.\n\nHere's what to check:\n\n1. **Bucket Policy**: Ensure the bucket policy explicitly allows the Lambda's IAM role ARN to perform `s3:PutObject` on the bucket and its objects. For example:\n   ```json\n   {\n     \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n     \"Statement\": [\n       {\n         \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n         \"Principal\": {\n           \"AWS\": \"arn:aws:iam::YOUR_ACCOUNT_ID:role/lambda-execution-role\"\n         },\n         \"Action\": \"s3:PutObject\",\n         \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::my-app-logs-bucket/*\"\n       }\n     ]\n   }\n   ```",
      "source": "target",
